{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>How shall I curse, whom El has not cursed.</b> Even when they were worthy of cursing on account of the deed of the calf, He did not cease from endearing them — the clouds of glory, the manna, and the well did not stop. And so it is written in Ezra (Nehemiah 9:18): ״אף כי עשו להם עגל מסכה ויאמרו זה אלהיך אשר העלך מארץ מצרים ויעשו נאצות גדולות״ — 'Even when they made themselves a molten calf and said, this is your Elohim who brought you up from the land of Egypt, and committed great provocations,' — ״ואתה ברחמיך הרבים לא עזבתם במדבר״ — 'and You in Your abundant compassion did not forsake them in the wilderness' — ״עמוד הענן לא סר מעליהם ביומם להנחותם בהדרך ואת עמוד האש בלילה להאיר להם ואת הדרך אשר ילכו בה״ — 'the pillar of cloud did not depart from above them by day to guide them on the way, and the pillar of fire by night to illuminate for them and the way they should go' — ״ורוחך הטובה נתת להשכילם ומנך לא מנעת מפיהם ומים נתת להם לצמאם״ — 'and Your good spirit You gave to make them understand, and Your manna You did not withhold from their mouth, and water You gave them for their thirst.'" "<b>And it is fitting</b> to interpret מה אקוב לא קבה אל — 'How shall I curse, whom El has not cursed' — as said concerning Jacob, who was called El, as it is written (Genesis 33:20): ״ויקרא לו אל אלהי ישראל״ — 'and he called it El, Elohei Yisrael.' And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: who called him El? Elohei Yisrael. And this is to say that even in the hour of His wrath, when He cursed, He did not curse except His anger (אפם). And 'How shall I be wrath — HaShem was not wrathful all these days'; and all my power and wisdom is only in the hour of His wrath."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The verse cited is from Nehemiah 9, which Rabbeinu Bahya attributes to 'Ezra' (Ezra-Nehemiah being traditionally associated with Ezra). The citation reference is given as נחמיה ט׳:י״ח."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:24.536714878Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}